---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Builds"
  description="Things I've built with Claude Code – MCP servers, multi-agent systems, SEO tools, and automations."
  currentSlug="builds"
>
  <div class="note-content">
    <h1>🔧 builds</h1>

    <p>45+ systems, 9 mcp servers, 17,000+ lines of python. all built with claude code since may 2025.</p>

    <h2>infrastructure</h2>

    <div class="activity-cards">
      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">01</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>9 custom mcp servers</h3>
          <p>9 servers that let claude read my email, update my calendar, pull analytics, and write google docs. 8,600 lines of python, 78 tools total.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">02</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>parathink 3.0</h3>
          <p>spawns 2–15 research agents that divide up work without duplicating each other. territory assignment, quality gates, 23-test verification suite. 1,141 lines.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">03</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>research architect</h3>
          <p>spawns 4–10 agents across 5 research dimensions – trends, players, data, risks, opportunities – then a synthesizer merges everything into one report.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>applications</h2>

    <div class="activity-cards">
      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">04</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>last30days</h3>
          <p>searches reddit, x, and the web for what's trending on any topic in the last 30 days. 3 api modes, deduplication, auto-caching.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">05</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>granola auto-sync</h3>
          <p>daemon that watches meeting transcripts, classifies them through claude haiku, files them to the right folder, and extracts action items. runs twice a day, zero input.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">06</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>youtube transcript retriever</h3>
          <p>839 lines, 4-layer fallback (youtube API → yt-dlp → live chat → local whisper). never fails to get a transcript.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">07</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>firecrawl cli</h3>
          <p>736-line python wrapper for web scraping. 7 commands, async polling, credit tracking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>seo tools</h2>

    <div class="activity-cards">
      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">08</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>geo content optimizer</h3>
          <p>optimizes content so AI search engines actually cite it. 6 parallel agents checking entity grounding, causal clarity, and structure. outputs branded docx.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">09</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>writing standards</h3>
          <p>417-line system for making AI writing undetectable. 12 core rules applied to every piece of output before delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">10</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>ahrefs validator</h3>
          <p>567-line API cost control system. column validation, error pattern library. prevents expensive API mistakes before they happen.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>shipped</h2>

    <div class="activity-cards">
      <a class="activity-card link" href="/umbra">
        <span class="activity-number">🌘</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>umbra</h3>
          <p>a chrome extension that lets any llm drive my signed-in browser, not just claude in chrome. pairs on a local key, runs in the background, nothing leaves the machine. on the chrome web store.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>the fun ones</h2>

    <div class="activity-cards">
      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">11</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>puppy status line</h3>
          <p>a weather-aware virtual dog that lives in my terminal. 150+ activities, multi-day storylines. solves nothing. it's delightful.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="activity-card static">
        <span class="activity-number">12</span>
        <div class="activity-info">
          <h3>serpent</h3>
          <p>1,867 lines, zero dependencies. procedural audio engine, particle system, 14 achievements, 7 themes. a snake game that got out of hand.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>this website</h2>

    <p>robertjohnlora.com itself – astro 5, tailwind v4, apple notes design. the interactive stuff lives in <a href="/play">play</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .activity-cards {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .activity-card {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      transition: all 0.2s ease;
    }

    .activity-card.static {
      cursor: default;
    }

    a.activity-card.link {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
    }

    a.activity-card.link:hover {
      border-color: var(--text-muted);
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }

    .activity-number {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      min-width: 24px;
    }

    .activity-info h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-primary);
    }

    .activity-info p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
